{"title":"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(2_seconds,_quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (2 seconds, quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Diana and Apollo each roll a standard die obtaining a number at random from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  What is the probability that Diana's number is larger than Apollo's number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1533c0bbc2f59f03ed04e167c2539e1fc33a62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{3} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{5}{12} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{4}{9} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{17}{36} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the probability of Diana rolling a number larger than Apollo's is the same as the probability of Apollo's being more than Diana's. If we denote this common probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5dcbc2ccdb6173ca1f288717a94335b26976b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2D+P($\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />Apollo=Diana<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2c68fc6ab8142a08deee07c35384b66071e884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />. Now all we need to do is find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e1f82fe070695d9510f8c7a458b5aa4fecd00e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P($\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" />Apollo=Diana<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/85852dfb3301b06f35017d1598f80915cce9a9ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"5\" height=\"18\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d91d485b3d42ab59402da1a27bc435291625ecc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6(6)=36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> possibilities total, and 6 of those have Apollo=Diana, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e1f82fe070695d9510f8c7a458b5aa4fecd00e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P($\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" />Apollo=Diana<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83fd59c9e97fbd45c44e7730d5835d6c5034fe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$)=\\frac{6}{36}=\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"37\" />. Going back to our first equation and solving for D, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c7fb78c9d69ceed9bb14c9c153fa1a341241f2d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2D+\\frac{1}{6}=1\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e867d9baa50945d5911cfa6b8eb8c5687c537020.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2D=\\frac{5}{6}\\]\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7be96a8bf53ed094a637ebf30878107b2b582e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D=\\frac{5}{12} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(B)}\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use simple casework to solve this problem too. There are six cases based on Apollo's Roll.\nApollo Rolls a 1: Diana could roll a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nApollo Rolls a 2: Diana could roll a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nApollo Rolls a 3: Diana could roll a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nApollo Rolls a 4: Diana could roll a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nApollo Rolls a 5: Diana could roll a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nApollo Rolls a 6: There are no successful outcomes.\nThe total amount of successful cases is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/817b24bd2b271b12d66c8c3f54e85fbc15d5e703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+4+3+2+1 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"14\" />. The total amount of possible cases is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/2/a82f8880e15a38fc13940e4cd65056eabca3e2bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6(6) = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, the probability of Diana rolling a bigger number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/480d656d9b2598764a9b45ec577031e0d18e8fbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{36} = \\frac{5}{12} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.282_seconds.2C_quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(2_seconds,_quick)\">Solution 3 (2 seconds, quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (2 seconds, quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define a \"win\" for Player 1 as rolling a greater number than Player 2. Because potential ties make up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0af542d70ceab4c3ca2f53654518dd6e09dd80f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{36}=\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"58\" height=\"37\" /> of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> combinations, Apollo and Diana \"split\" the wins in the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47b82abaed0eb123194fe422cf0cd902de6e2a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />. By symmetry, each person wins half of these, so the probability Diana wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58dae1e3275e49c1e364bb01b6340e7a4fe4e370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{5}{6}}{2}=\\frac{5}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"42\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e1a33aa98a1c90339a098b97ad62b20f590fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME\" title=\"1995 AJHSME\">1995 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1995\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017185158\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 248/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1967/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6712/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.496      1 Template:AJHSME_box\n100.00%    7.496      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10156:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017185158 and revision id 281757. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}